==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{LL.}} {{term|sphincter|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|σφιγκτήρ||band, contractile muscle|tr=sphinktēr|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, from {{term|σφίγγω||I bind tight|tr=sphingō|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}. Compare [[Sphinx]], "the strangler".

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{anatomy}} A [[ringlike]] [[band]] of [[muscle]] that surrounds a bodily opening, [[constrict]]ing and [[relax]]ing as required for normal [[physiological]] functioning.

